1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,720
Same 50,000 VND morning coffee sitting on the counter.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:14,410
Why does tapping a credit card cost the shop 2.2%, while scanning a plastic QR stand pays 100% in three seconds flat?

3
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:24,960
When you tap a credit card, the POS terminal sends a pull instruction to advance money from your issuing bank for 45 days, triggering interchange fees.

4
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:29,730
Scanning QR pushes cash straight out of your existing CASA checking balance.

5
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:35,880
No bank advances a 45-day loan or absorbs default risk, so standard transfer fees drop to zero.

6
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:42,090
Pre-funded interbank collateral lets the shop's bank credit the full 50,000 VND to Account 112 right away.

7
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:46,450
Commercial banks never ship cash for individual 50,000 VND coffees all afternoon.

8
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:51,810
Millions of two-way transfers offset each other, moving just one net reserve difference at the Central Bank at session close.

9
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:57,670
Across 10,000,000 VND in daily cafe sales, cards return 9,780,000 VND two days later.

10
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:03,340
QR keeps the extra 220,000 VND at the counter while holding cheap 0.1% CASA deposits inside banks.

11
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:09,100
At familiar neighborhood counters, scanning QR helps shops keep every dong.

12
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:16,130
When ordering from unfamiliar remote sellers online, remember QR works like cash with zero Chargeback rights.
